    "updated_at": "2026-11-20T18:36:11Z",
    "body": "Looks already fixed on upstream/main d113deaae: the issue's steps do not reproduce without a change. Suggest closing; the maintainer decides.\n\nEvidence:\n\n- I wrote an app-level test with the issue's setup. It uses the finished and blank meridians, 48 segments, `lathe.mch`, `TN-1600-0R8`, the blank as from-model stock with raw stock only on, and the three operations C1, T1 and M1 with the issue's numbers.\n- On upstream/main d113deaae, all three operations have no blocking finding. The Fanuc Lathe post writes the program.\n- I then put back the three sim files from before PR #2911 (`crates/sim/src/solid_rest.rs`, `crates/sim/src/stock_sim/scan_hidden.rs`, `crates/sim/src/stock_sim/scan_turned.rs`, from `30f308211^1`). The same test then fails with the issue's exact text:\n\n```text\n(\"M1\", [\"finish envelope near move 235: 0.0073 mm gouge, 2.2543 mm rest\"])\n```\n\n- The issue base `58cb641ca` does not contain PR #2911 (merge `30f308211`, issue #2880). PR #2911 changed the turned hidden-rest window law. That change is the likely fix.\n\nI released the claim. I did not open a PR. If the maintainer wants the pin test on main, it is a small new file in `crates/app/tests/`; a worker can add it with this setup.\n",
